## Default rules

1. **update** (same URL) is the default: the search intent is the same, so the existing page —
   with its links and history — is fixed. A new article that `superseded` this one, while this
   body has no link to it, is also a reason to update (add the link).
2. **new** (a new article; this one stays as it is) when:
   - (a) the top queries moved to a different intent than the article serves;
   - (b) the point in time is the content (people search per year, edition or version);
   - (c) fixing it would change the article's topic or target reader.
3. **none** when there is nothing to fix: the facts still hold and a metrics drop looks seasonal
   or competitive. Never refresh only to change a date.

